{"name":"Little Blue Box","hex":"#8ac5ba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"little","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Small, not large, limited, particularly:","Small, limited in size."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Not much.","Not at all."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"box","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Buamu."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Senses relating to a three-dimensional object or space.\n A cuboid space; a cuboid container, often with a hinged lid.","A cuboid space; a cuboid container, often with a hinged lid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/box"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue box","blocks":[{"text":"A blue box is an electronic device that produces tones used to generate the in-band signaling tones formerly used within the North American long-distance telephone network to send line status and called number information over voice circuits. During that period, charges for long-distance calling were commonplace and could be significant, depending on the time, duration and destination of the call. A blue box device allowed illicit users to circumvent these charges, placing long-distance calls that would be billed to another number or dismissed entirely by the telecom company's billing system as an incomplete call. A number of similar \"color boxes\" were also created to control other aspects of the phone network, a practice called \"phreaking\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Blue_Box_at_the_Powerhouse_Museum.jpg/330px-Blue_Box_at_the_Powerhouse_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_box","wikidata":"Q586874"},{"title":"Box","blocks":[{"text":"A box is a container with rigid sides used for the storage or transportation of its contents. Most boxes have flat, parallel, rectangular sides. Boxes can be very small or very large and can be used for a variety of purposes, from functional to decorative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif/lossy-page1-330px-L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Box","wikidata":"Q188075"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif/lossy-page1-500px-L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai